  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 139 AM CDT Fri Aug 21 2026\n\nThe upper ridge will flatten a bit early next week, but also shift \ndirectly over our region. This will likely bring the peak of the \ncurrent heat wave Monday/Tuesday with nearly all locations at or \nabove 100 degrees. The ridge shifts west late in the week helping \ndecrease temperatures by a few degrees. This will also open the door \nfor a few storms to move in from the TX Panhandle. Rain chances \nremain low (<30%), but at least there's a chance!",
